@1   = ~chriz-bg-kits requires BG2:EE or EET with EEex v1.2.0+ (extra_pattern_dbs + M___EEex.lua).~
@2   = ~chriz-bg-kits replaces ArtisansKitpack and BardicWonders and cannot be installed alongside them.~
@3   = ~Requires Component 100 (Core EEex Kit Kernel) to be installed first.~

@100 = ~Core EEex Kit Kernel (Weapon Usability, Multiclass Kit Proficiencies, Global Non-Warrior Proficiency APR, Bard Spells, Strength Floor)~
@110 = ~Forgotten Realms Racial Class, Kit & Multiclass Rules (Recommended)~
@111 = ~Unlock All Classes, Kits, Dual-Classes & Multiclasses for All Races~
@112 = ~Racial Class, Kit & Multiclass Rules~
@200 = ~Cleric Overhaul: Priest of Tempus~
@210 = ~Sorcerer Kit: Stonefire Sorcerer~
@220 = ~Druid Kit: Elementalist~
@300 = ~Standalone Fighter Kit: Bloodrager~
@310 = ~Bard Overhaul: Jester & Skald~
@320 = ~Core Kit & HLA Fixes (Archer Called Shot, Physical Hardiness, Resist Magic, Deathblows, Dual-Class Kit Names)~

@201 = ~Holy Power~
@202 = ~Holy Power
Through this prayer, the Priest of Tempus channels divine battle-prowess, gaining Fighter THAC0 progression, temporary Strength floor scaling up to 21 at level 15 (without lowering stronger Strength buffs), and +1 Hit Point per level (max 20). Does not stack with other transformation magic.~
@203 = ~Chaos of Battle~
@204 = ~Chaos of Battle
The Priest of Tempus unleashes battle-luck across allies (+1 to +3 Luck) while cursing nearby enemies (-1 to -3 THAC0 and Saving Throws, Save vs. Spell negates).~
@205 = ~PRIEST OF TEMPUS: Champions of the Lord of Battles relish honorable melee combat and shun sneaky divination magic.
Advantages:
- Automatically receives 1 Battle Axe proficiency at 1st level in addition to starting pips, and may place 2 pips in Long Sword, Battle Axe, Crossbow, standard cleric weapons, and all fighting styles.
- Gains +1/2 attack per round when wielding a weapon in which the priest holds 2 or more proficiency pips (without double-stacking on Warrior multiclasses).
- Casts Chaos of Battle and an enhanced non-lowering Holy Power.
Disadvantages:
- Divination Toll: Tempus strips all Divination priest spells from the cleric's spellbook.~

@301 = ~Enrage~
@302 = ~Enrage
Enters a blood-fueled frenzy for 5 rounds (+2 melee THAC0, +2 melee damage, -2 Armor Class penalty, +15 temporary Hit Points with no end-of-rage backlash), shielding the mind against Charm, Fear, Hold, Sleep, and Stun. Each melee hit sustains the frenzy up to a 10-round maximum (20 rounds with Extend Rage). When Enrage ends, the Bloodrager is Winded for 5 rounds (-2 THAC0, -2 damage, +2 AC penalty).~
@303 = ~Extend Rage~
@304 = ~Extend Rage (HLA)
Doubles the maximum sustained duration of Enrage from 10 rounds to 20 rounds.~
@305 = ~bloodrager~
@306 = ~Bloodrager~
@307 = ~BLOODRAGER: A savage frontline warrior whose fury intensifies as wounds accumulate.
Advantages:
- In Extremis: Gains +1 melee damage and +1 Save vs. Death at <76%, <50%, and <26% Hit Points (doubled while Enraged); at level 14+, each threshold also grants +5% physical resistance (doubled to +10%/+20%/+30% while Enraged).
- May Enrage 1/day per 4 levels (focused mind-shield, temporary Hit Points, melee-hit duration refresh up to hard cap).
Disadvantages:
- Suffers a permanent -4 THAC0 penalty with ranged weapons.
- Cannot place proficiency pips in or equip ranged missile weapons (Crossbow, Longbow, Shortbow, Dart, Sling).~

@401 = ~Piercing Mockery~
@402 = ~Piercing Mockery
The Jester's song unnerves enemies (Save vs. Spell with scaling penalty up to -4), inflicting Confusion, Slow at high levels, and -1/-2 penalties to THAC0 and Saving Throws.~
@403 = ~Heckle~
@404 = ~Heckle
Mocks a single foe (-2 THAC0, -2 Armor Class, 35% spell failure for 3 rounds, Save vs. Spell negates).~
@405 = ~Mad Ramble~
@406 = ~Mad Ramble
Broadcasts disorienting nonsense around the Jester (25% spell failure and -1 Luck to nearby enemies, Save vs. Spell negates).~
@407 = ~The Fool's Journey~
@408 = ~The Fool's Journey (HLA)
Permanent +1 Luck, +2 Saving Throws, and a non-stacking aura granting allies +1 Luck and +1 THAC0.~
@409 = ~JESTER: Uses biting mockery (Heckle, Mad Ramble, Piercing Mockery) and un-nerfed IWD spell progression up to 7th level.~
@410 = ~SKALD: Inspires allies in combat and may place up to 2 proficiency pips in every weapon and fighting style, while casting BG2 bard spells up to 6th level.~

@501 = ~Hardiness (HLA): Grants 40% resistance to all physical damage types for 1 turn.~
@502 = ~Resist Magic (HLA): Sets Magic Resistance to a minimum floor of 50% for 4 rounds without lowering higher existing Magic Resistance.~
@503 = ~Deathblow (HLA): Automatically slays struck creatures of 12 Hit Dice or fewer for 2 rounds.~
@504 = ~Greater Deathblow (HLA): Automatically slays struck creatures of 16 Hit Dice or fewer for 2 rounds.~

@511 = ~Mage~
@512 = ~Fighter~
